  "sun_energy_fraction": 0.7583,
  "notes": "Sunny clear late-afternoon/morning meadow with green grass, bushes and large deciduous trees around the horizon (Germany); sun visible, white balance ~5300K, 27 EV range. Conventions VERIFIED in Blender 5.2 Cycles (source kernel/camera/projection.h + a test render): u = 0.5 - atan2(dir.y, dir.x)/(2*pi), v = 1 - acos(dir.z)/pi (v measured from image bottom). So image centre u=0.5 faces +X; u=0.25 faces +Y; u=0.75 faces -Y. Unrotated, the sun is at azimuth -36.17 deg (CCW from +X, i.e. towards +X/-Y) and elevation 26.98 deg, direction [0.7194, -0.526, 0.4537]. With TexCoord(Generated) -> Mapping(type POINT, Rotation Z = theta) -> Environment Texture, the sun appears at azimuth (-36.17 - theta). To put the sun at world azimuth alpha (deg, CCW from +X): theta = -36.17 - alpha (verified by render). Sun energy is concentrated in ~25-30 pixels at 4K; leave the HDRI as sole light or add a Sun lamp matching this direction (angle ~0.5 deg) and clamp/limit the HDRI if fireflies appear."
 },
